---
const pains = [
  {
    title: "No FFmpeg pipeline",
    body: "IP cameras already speak RTSP. A webcam does not. The usual fix is piping frames through FFmpeg or GStreamer into a separate media server.",
  },
  {
    title: "No extra hardware",
    body: "Buying a dedicated IP camera for a job a laptop or phone you already own can do is the expensive way around a missing URL.",
  },
  {
    title: "No helper process",
    body: "camrtsp opens the OS camera API, encodes with the OS hardware encoder, and serves RTSP from the same process.",
  },
];
---

<section id="why" class="border-b border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-copper">Why camrtsp</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      VLC, OBS, NVRs, and Home Assistant already know how to pull an RTSP URL.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-paper-dim">
      A laptop webcam or a phone camera does not. camrtsp is the missing publisher:
      it gives those viewers a URL they already understand.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      {pains.map((item) => (
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-ink-2 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-dim">{item.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line">
      <div class="min-w-[40rem]">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 border-b border-line bg-ink-2 px-5 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-mute">
          <span>You have</span>
          <span>You need</span>
          <span>camrtsp gives you</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 divide-x divide-line text-sm">
          <p class="px-5 py-5 text-paper-dim">A Mac, Windows PC, or Android phone with a camera</p>
          <p class="px-5 py-5 text-paper-dim">A URL other software can subscribe to</p>
          <p class="px-5 py-5 font-mono text-copper">rtsp://host:8554/camera</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
